ar. To me, even 20 years seems too short. Congressman.\par \par \uc2 REP. JIM BANKS (R-IN): Well, that's right, President Trump has been clear every step of the way, Iran can never have a nuclear weapon. I mean, that's what these negotiations are all about. That's what this war is about. Any terms that fall short of that is unsuccessful. And by the way, Laura, President Trump every step of the way has warned the Iranians. He's given them timelines. He's told them exactly what he's going to do, drop the nuclear program, stop funneling money to terrorist proxy groups and open the Straits, or we're going to bomb the hell out of you. And President Trump has kept his word every step of the way.\par \par \uc2 The Iranians know that and that's why they're begging to come back to the table to continue these negotiations. I have a sense that we're on the -- we're in the final stages of all of this. Vice President Vance's efforts last week was a -- I thought a good signal, a good sign that these negotiations will move in the right direction as the Iranians realize what stands in front of them next Tuesday, when this ceasefire is over, come to their senses, come back to the table, drop the nuclear program forever.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Most Americans still think we are the good guys in this, Congressman, but some of the media elites seem to be on the fence. Check this out.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 THOMAS FRIEDMAN, FOREIGN AFFAIRS COLUMNIST, THE NEW YORK TIMES: The problem is, I really don't want to see Bibi Netanyahu or Donald Trump politically strengthened by this war, because they are two awful human beings. They are terrible, terrible people doing terrible things to America, standing in the world, and Israel standing in the world. And so I really find myself torn. I want to see Iran militarily defeated, but I do not want to see these two terrible people strengthened.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: OK, he's torn, Congressman. So, dump the mullahs who are -- take -- take glee in torturing and executing dissidents, or a duly elected President of the United States, in his best judgment, that's a hard call for Tom Friedman.\par \par \uc2 BANKS: Well, there is nothing more demoralizing, by the way, to our troops who are in the fight, who are fighting in a war to keep America safe and secure than to watch the Democrats and the media cheer against the commander-in-chief and the very efforts that they're a part of. I mean, it's shameful that they would -- that they would cheer against our troops in that kind of a way. So, shame -- shame on the Democrats for that and the media for joining them.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Senator, do you think the president should at least threaten to not go to this Beijing Summit, given these reports of China's support for Iran in this conflict, and cargo ships reportedly with Chinese material landing over the weekend in, you know, in the region.\par \par \uc2 BANKS: It's a key -- it's a great point, because 80 percent of Iran's oil goes to China. So, we're -- the blockade is weakening China, as President Trump is seeking a better trade deal with our biggest enemy to put American workers first. So, it's a great point, but I think it gives the president even more leverage when he goes to Beijing.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Senator, thank you very much. Great to see you. And coming up, a conservative journalist attacked by a violent anti-ICE mob. Coming up.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: What are anti-ICE activists hiding? Independent journalist Savanah Hernandez showed up in Minneapolis to try find out.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Oh, God. Hang on. (INAUDIBLE) come here today to, you know, try and interview people. I came here to simply observe.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: No, no. You don't know who the (BLEEP).\par \par \uc2 (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The TPUSA Frontlines reporter found out that the stop hate crowd is the most vicious bunch you could ever come face to face with.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Get the (BLEEP) out of here. Get the (BLEEP) out of here.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Get away from me\par \par \uc2 (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And the attack on Hernandez turned into a family affair, entered the dead, Chris Ostrashoko, known on social media as the Minnesota Angry Man.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Stop pushing me.\par \par \uc2 (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Hernandez is about 5'4" or so, and this beast with the bulging eyes appeared to violently shove her to the ground. You can't see his eyes for some reason in that, but suffice it to say his big bulging eyes. Now she wasn't hurt worse. Yeah. Well, she's lucky for that.\par \par \uc2 Now at that point she was just trying to get out of there, but the daughter returned to the scene.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Leave me alone. I'm trying to leave.\par \par \uc2 (INAUDIBLE)\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The three raving maniacs were arrested and we're still working to find out the charges, and the FBI has opened up an investigation. Here exclusively to tell her story, Savanah Hernandez, TPUSA Frontlines reporter.\par \par \uc2 Savanah, I was very worried about you when I saw this video. It's very scary. I was standing exactly where you were standing back in January. These people are crazy. Why did it escalate so quickly?\par \par \uc2 SAVANAH HERNANDEZ, FRONTLINES TPUSA REPORTER: Well, let's make no mistake, Laura, this escalated because they found out that I work for Turning Point USA. This isn't the first time that I have been confronted and assaulted at this point for journalism on the streets of the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 But since Charlie Kirk's assassination, this is now the third time that people have come up to me, after I have not been interviewing, not been engaging, but simply being on the street and filming the protest, figured out I work for Turning Point USA, and have made a point to confront me, to threaten me, to harass me, and now brutally assault me to prove a point.\par \par \uc2 So that's why this escalated, Laura. I wasn't interviewing anybody. I wasn't engaging with anybody. I was, and I apologize, this is the first time I'm talking about this assault and I'm scared to report, Laura, this is my job. It's what I've been doing for the last six years. And I'm terrified to do my job.\par \par \uc2 I can't even interview people properly on the street because I got brutally assaulted and pushed to the ground by a 250-pound man for simply going and reporting on anti-ICE activities. I made a point not to engage, Laura, because I know the left-wing is violent.\par \par \uc2 They assassinated Charlie Kirk last year and now they're coming for each and every single Turning Point USA employee because they know they can get away with it, because the local jurisdictions aren't going to charge them.\par \par \uc2 Now, luckily, the sheriffs are planning on bringing forward charges, I hope. I did tell them I wanted to press charges. This has been elevated to both the DOJ and the DHS. They're opening an investigation as well. But I'm horrified, Laura. I'm horrified.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, this is the United States of America. You were just standing there. And I know exactly how you feel because they surrounded me, the same exact way, and they start screaming in your ear and, you know, you stuck around there a little longer than I did because I got in my car because I didn't want to deal with this.\par \par \uc2 But this is their M.O. They don't want anyone there because they don't want anyone knowing the truth about how many of them are paid, how this is organized, who's funding it, and what they are really all