ked journalists. Well, they also attacked sworn law enforcement officers. We're living in a country now where an ICE officer gets attacked daily. These protests, these attacks, not only happened where Sarah was, they also happened in Los Angeles, Portland, Chicago. It's an ongoing dilemma.\par \par \uc2 And that's why I'm grateful the FBI is stepping in, DOJ is going to seek prosecution on this, because at this point, I don't trust any local jury in a sanctuary jurisdiction. I'd much rather see the Feds pick it up and charge it with a federal crime because the sentence is going to be a lot more stringent and it sends a strong message.\par \par \uc2 But we cannot give up on this. We've got to keep prosecuting these people. 18 USC 111, you know, interference of soul, record high number of prosecutions. We've got to continue down that path and hold these people accountable. We cannot accept this as a norm in the United States of America.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And Savanah, we don't want anyone injured who are at these protests, whatever we want to call them, protests, sometimes they feel like festivals, depending on what the weather is like. But no one should be hurt for exercising their First Amendment rights.\par \par \uc2 And Savanah, are you satisfied, in your view, that the FBI will be able to handle this?\par \par \uc2 HERNANDEZ: I hope they do. Again, the DHS is involved as well. And I hope that, you know, the full force of the federal government is utilized against these people, to send a message to all of the radical left-wing who have been targeting journalists for years, attacking us, harassing us, censoring us and silencing us. I really hope that a message is sent here with this and it's followed through with.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Savanah, please stay out there doing what you're doing. Tom, when people are screaming in your ear or blowing a whistle in your ear, they do it to ICE agents, when they're not trying to run them over with their vehicles, they're doing it to ICE agents, that, in and of itself, is an assault.\par \par \uc2 I mean, you lose your hearing or a damaged hearing, but that's part of routine. And for their part, they say, your ICE agents are killing our people. We're just blowing a whistle or shoving someone to the ground.\par \par \uc2 HOMAN: Well, it's not acceptable. It's interference. It's impeding because it prevents them from doing what they're doing, whether they're busy dealing with this protester that turned criminal. No, bad guys are getting away. So, you're exactly right, it is interference, we need to prosecute more of these cases.\par \par \uc2 And I apologize to Savannah. I got her name mixed up. But, you know, she's a patriot. She went out there, a female in that crowd, to report to the American people the truth. But the left doesn't want to hear the truth, but we're going to keep pushing.\par \par \uc2 Laura, if it wasn't for this network, the American people wouldn't hear the truth. But members of Congress, every day, I've been up on Hill negotiating DHS shutdown. They don't want to reform ICE. They want to shut it down. And they talk about ICE making arrests in schools and churches and hospitals. We've never made an arrest inside of a hospital. We've never made arrests inside of a church. But I watched a TV show last week, some medical show, and they showed ICE agents coming into emergency and arresting somebody that was getting ready for surgery.\par \par \uc2 The whole left is misinforming the American people, and that's why you see the hate in their rhetoric, because all these people are lying about what the men and women of ICE and Border Patrol do. So, thank God we have network like Fox News that's going to put out the truth to the American people.\par \par \uc2 I just wish more networks were honest and talk about the real job that ICE is doing, and most importantly, what they're not doing.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And Tom, meanwhile, we have illegal aliens hammering to death American citizens, bludgeoning them to death, slitting their throats at bus stops, groping them in high school hallways. We're showing that horrible case from Fort Myers, Florida, Haitian illegal.\par \par \uc2 And if it weren't for ICE trying to get these people out, if the word for the open border, bringing all these illegals into the country, I mean, would have a lot more people alive in our country or not brutalized.\par \par \uc2 HOMAN: You're exactly right, and that's why I came back the second time out of retirement because for four years I woke up every day pissed off about what the Biden administration did to our border and not letting ICE do their job.\par \par \uc2 And I still wake up angry every day when I see stories like this because, again, they're shutting down DHS because they don't want ICE to do their job. They're protecting criminal aliens over the men and women who wear that badge and gun, and over the American citizens who are in danger in these sanctuary cities.\par \par \uc2 So, it's -- the world is upside down. But, in look, I've worked for the greatest president my lifetime. We're not giving up. We're pushing forward. We are going to have a mass deportation operation. We'll keep that border secure. We're going keep doing our job despite the hate, despite the rhetoric.\par \par \uc2 And, you know, God bless the Angel families. Another reason I came back from retirement. I met hundreds of them. Their stories will never get old.\par \par \uc2 But here's the issue, Laura. We're talking about this one attack in Florida. We'll be talking about something else next week and something else the following week. Every member of Congress, it should be non-partisan issue.\par \par \uc2 Let ICE enforce the immigration law and make this country safer again. Every public safety threat we take off the street makes this country safe. Every illegal alien we take off the street prevents a crime in the future. So let us enforce the law. We're going to do it all