e look outside the beltway SPECIAL REPORT. We'll be right back.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. HAKEEM JEFFRIES, (D-NY) HOUSE MINORITY LEADER: Republicans are being crushed. Donald Trump's approval rating is underwater, including as it relates to the economy.\par \par \uc2 HOWARD LUTNICK, COMMERCE SECRETARY: The United States of America, with its $30 trillion economy, grow in the six percent range, and no one thought that was possible.\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP, (R) U.S. PRESIDENT: We're going to be announcing next week I think sometime, Scott and Howard and everybody, we're going to be announcing the head of the Fed.\par \par \uc2 Did we make the right choice? You know, a lot of times you make a choice, you think it's good, and it turns out to be not good. But with the help of the Fed we can hit numbers that have never been hit before.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: President Trump in his cabinet meeting today focusing a lot on the U.S. economy. Did not hear from the Department of Homeland Security Secretary Kristi Noem, did not take questions. A little bit different cabinet hearing than we have said before.\par \par \uc2 The FOX News polls, the new ones out, what should President Trump's top priorities be? And you see there overwhelmingly, economy, jobs, inflation, prices. Obviously, some adamant Democrats there are resign and quit. Unite the country gets eight percent.\par \par \uc2 Let's bring in our panel, FOX News political analyst Reince Priebus we welcome on board, FOX News senior political analyst Juan Williams, and "Politico" White House bureau chief Dasha Burns. Dasha, was there a signal in who spoke and the focus?\par \par \uc2 DASHA BURNS, "POLITICO": You know the president knows how to put on a show, and he is often pretty deliberate with this kind of thing. Look, there is a lot of frustration among Republicans both on the Hill and in the White House that immigration has gone fr