e to be taken very seriously. George Soros was the most effective Left-wing activist of this century, and his son is going to carry that torch. And any of those people on that Instagram, consider them bought off.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Alex, you're the best. Thank you very much. And while Newsom is paling around at Davos with his BFF, it looks like he has a new problem on his hands. Independent Journalist Nick Shirley was on the Hill today testifying about the fraud and abuse he's helped uncover in Minnesota, and says Newsom, whoa, better watch out.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Have you seen any signs there that sort of are similar to what aroused your suspicions in Minnesota?\par \par \uc2 NICK SHIRLEY, INDEPENDENT JOURNALIST: Yes, and fraud in California might be worse than the fraud in Minnesota.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: What makes you say that?\par \par \uc2 SHIRLEY: Well, $24 billion went missing for homelessness. They've been trying to build this train for years, yet there's hardly anything to prove for that. Fires.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Nick Shirley is here exclusively to tell us more. Nick, what you've discovered in Minnesota finally made people pay attention. So what are your plans to expose fraud in California?\par \par \uc2 SHIRLEY: Well, I got to be a little secret about that, because you don't know, you wouldn't be -- you'd be surprised to know how dangerous exposing fraud is, I never thought fraud, exposing fraud become something so controversial. But yes, fraud will be exposed in California, will be exposed all across the United States, because we're learning that there's so much fraud that's taking place, whether it'd be through daycares or these projects like that high speed light rail that Newsom has been trying to build for years.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Are you surprised how easy it is. It's like taking candy from a baby, the federal government or state government, when you have these politicians and career bureaucrats who really have no incentive to stop the fraud or actually have a political incentive to keep the gravy train rolling here.\par \par \uc2 SHIRLEY: Well, the only reason it could be so easy is because somebody has to be getting kickbacks. Because if anyone else was to give away a million dollars to your next door neighbor or to some other Rando, you'd want to know where that money is going. And so it has to be, there has to be some sort of reason why they're allowing this fraud to happen. It's not just because it's some random NGO. Somebody has to be getting kickbacks.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, you said it's dangerous for you out there. We've seen the videos and people screaming at you and so forth. But what have you had to deal with?\par \par \uc2 SHIRLEY: I mean, your house gets doxed. People try to hack in your social media accounts. People start calling your family members, and you have to go everywhere. 24/7 security. It's just not the same anymore. And it kind of sucks to be honest, because, like I said, I was just exposing fraud, and then you see all this hatred come at you for doing a giant public service for America where the majority of Americans are super happy. I'd say 99 percent, but then you have that crazy 1 percent that just get super upset because they're the fraudsters.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So given what you've exposed, Nick, what do you say to young conservatives who want to make a difference out there and see parts of their country slipping away?\par \par \uc2 SHIRLEY: I think the biggest thing is knowing that there is absolute truth in this world, and the truth of this world is fraud, is fraud, and fraud is bad, for example. And you could go and name some other truths as well, but when you know that what you're doing is right, you really shouldn't have to fear anything. And so, like me, I don't fear it, because I know I'm not doing anything wrong, because I know I'm seeking the truth. And 