ses. Twenty percent decline in that, that's 20,000 lives here in the United States of America that this president has saved. Think about the people, the criminals he's getting out of this country. The lives he's saving by doing that.\par \par \uc2 The wars he's ended around the world. The lives he's saved by doing that. I would argue this president has probably saved more lives around the world than anyone else single-handedly in my lifetime.\par \par \uc2 But the Democrats are going to continue down this path. And the problem they're also going to have is whenever the one big beautiful bill comes into effect in full by this, you know, spring and summer, as all the experts have predicted, they're going to have to stop talking about affordability.\par \par \uc2 So, get ready for more of this craziness to ramp up. They're going to sling a lot of insults around because they have nothing else to run on, and I hope the American people are paying close attention.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, and the funny thing is that you have all these former Trump officials who I never even met in the White House in the first Trump term, but I guess they had some role. Stephanie Grisham, I wouldn't recognize her if I saw her on the street, but she's like, oh, the Trump speech shows us that he's slipping. Oh, that shows that we need to -- you know, I'm just paraphrasing, 25th Amendment.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: Yeah. Well, all you need to know is that close to 90 percent, I think, of the signatures given during the Biden administration were done via auto pen. This president that we have right now, the 47th, has all of his faculties about him.\par \par \uc2 He literally had a three-hour delay getting to Davos last night because there was a problem with the plane. He went there, he schooled every single person in that audience about how they ought to be running their countries, about why America is back. You saw it. I loved every single second of this.\par \par \uc2 He exuded strength on the