rs. I think those statements were not in character, and he has apologized. I wish other people in public life would sincerely apologize for stuff. So no, I still am a supporter.\par \par \uc2 HOFF (voice over): From the nation's highest office to the Virginia delegate level, Republicans are calling for Jones to drop out, as is the Commonwealth's Fraternal Order of Police, saying in a statement yesterday, "The men and women of law enforcement worked tirelessly to combat the violence you wished on a fellow Virginian and his family."\par \par \uc2 Jones has expressed regret over the messages, adding, "I believe that violent rhetoric has no place in our politics." His Republican opponent, current Attorney General \uc2 Jason Miyares\uc2 , saying today, he is not buying it.\par \par \uc2 JASON MIYARES\uc2 , ATTORNEY GENERAL OF VIRGINIA: He is saying he is sorry because he's trying to save his political career.\par \par \uc2 HOFF (voice over): It remains to be seen what kind of impact this scandal will have on the state's gubernatorial race.\par \par \uc2 WINSOME EARLE-SEARS, LIEUTENANT GOVERNOR, VIRGINIA: I'm calling on \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2  to do what she should.\par \par \uc2 HOFF (voice over): Republican lieutenant governor, Winsome Earle-Sears is running against former Democratic Congresswoman \uc2 Abigail Spanberger\uc2 , who condemned Jones' texts but has not called for him to drop out.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 HOFF (on camera): Now, any candidate dropping out at this point would prove complicated election day is November 4th. Early voting has already started, and Virginia code requires at least 60 days' notice to put a replacement nominee's name on the ballot. Gillian.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: All right. Alexandria Hoff here in the D.C. newsroom for us tonight. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 Alarming new information. Coming into the newsroom tonight about the prevalence and the dangers of driving while high. New research out indicates more than 40 