th the vice president, national security advisor, and he would strongly prefer the report not, not be disseminated. Thanks for understanding." The email states it was signed by a redacted name, but with the title PDB briefer. Of course, that stands for presidential daily briefing.\par \par \uc2 No reaction from the Biden team as yet, though we have put in a request.\par \par \uc2 Also tonight, a senior CIA official tells FOX News Digital it's extremely rare and unusual and inappropriate to go outside the intel community and inquire with the White House on the dissemination of a particular report, something you know all too well, Gillian.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: All right, Kevin Corke in the newsroom for us here in D.C. tonight. Thank you.\par \par \uc2 CORKE: You bet.\par \par \uc2 TURNER: Well, coming up next, the panel on the dramatic exchanges in that Senate hearing featuring the attorney general earlier and the government shutdown that is now paralyzing Washington.\par \par \uc2 First, here's a look at what some of our FOX affiliates across the country are covering tonight. FOX 40 in Sacramento, California's Highway Patrol is investigating a helicopter crash that left three people in critical condition. It happened Monday evening in east Sacramento. The fire department says bystanders there helped lift the helicopter off of one of those victims.\par \par \uc2 And this WFXT out of Boston. Karen Read's attorneys file court documents demanding the immediate return of her cell phones from a special prosecutor who is holding them as part of an ongoing witness intimidation investigation. Read's lawyers called the action a fishing expedition intended to punish and harass her. Read was acquitted in June of second degree murder in the death of her police officer boyfriend.\par \par \uc2 This is a live look at Louisville. one of the big stories there tonight from WDRB, Louisville obtains a franchise in the United Football League. The Louisville Kings will begin play in the 