tors try to find a compromise to reopen the government.\par \par \uc2 Senior congressional correspondent Chad Pergram is following all the action. He is on Capitol Hill tonight.\par \par \uc2 CHAD PERGRAM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONGRESSIONAL CORRESPONDENT (voice over): Tension builds as the shutdown barrels toward a third day.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOHN THUNE\uc2  (R-SD): I realize that my Democrat colleagues are facing pressure from members of their far-left base, but they are playing a losing game here.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): Reopening government requires several Senate Democrats to side with the GOP.\par \par \uc2 BERNIE MORENO (R-OH): We need five more, and they can do it tomorrow.\par \par \uc2 And we can reopen this government for the American people.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): Bipartisan Senate negotiations continue off stage. Senators want government funded, but also aim to shore up Obamacare subsidies.\par \par \uc2 MARTHA MACCALLUM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL ANCHOR: And on temporary protection status during COVID.\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 SEN. CHRIS COONS (D-DE): But I'm not going to vote to reopen the government, until I see a way that we can do that.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): Some Republicans worry about Obamacare price spikes.\par \par \uc2 REP. JEFFERSON VAN DREW (R-NJ): There are some folks in what is the new part of the Republican Party, which is blue collar workers.\par \par \uc2 We have to be careful how we do this. We just shouldn't cut it. We should make sure we use a scalpel and not a sledgehammer.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): But even if senators forge a deal, the plan may die in the House.\par \par \uc2 REP. TOM COLE (R-OK): Republicans have spent most of their careers being against Obamacare. Why would they expand it and add a subsidy on top of a subsidy?\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): Republicans believe Democrats may face political consequences for the shutdown.\par \par \uc2 REP. STEVE SCALISE