suggesting. And secondly, we know now from "The Wall Street Journal" reporting that Trump's name was in those files, and he was told about it.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: FOX has confirmed that the attorney general did tell him, but also told him that it did not -- it doesn't have to be a bad thing and a list to be in.\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: Again, there is a long list of names associated with this.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: But we don't know, Olivia. We just don't know.\par \par \uc2 BEAVERS: We don't know. And I think that that's why you are seeing this escalating push on Capitol Hill for records to be released. And the longer that they put it off, like they are punting it or not revealing records that could, while still not releasing the names of these women, be released, Republicans are already being asked about it on the campaign trail.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: We dealt with this about things we don't know for a year-plus on the Russia investigation. Now we are starting to know something.\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: I honestly believe the Democrats are making a mistake here. I think that by leaning into this as much as they are, they are doing something that is designed to get under President Trump's skin but is not actually something that connects with the American people or something that they care about that much. And I think that that's not because it isn't important for us to know. It is. But I also think that it's something that is a distraction from the issues that will actually win them back votes.\par \par \uc2 BAIER: All right, panel, thank you.\par \par \uc2 And finally tonight, a special day.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We'll have panels, we'll have a place on the convention floor as well as the lodge. So we are really full 360 opportunity here.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: This is intense. Tens of thousands of fans descending on San Diego for ComiCon. Have you seen this thing, a four-day pop culture spectacle featuring updates on new science fiction movies, TV shows, "Star Wars," Indiana Jones, executive -- \uc2 George Lucas\uc2 , one of the headline guests. The convention has exclusive merchandise, comic book art, exhibits from iconic science fiction brands. Are any of you guys going to that?\par \par \uc2 DOMENECH: I've been there.\par \par \uc2 (LAUGHTER)\par \par \uc2 BAIER: You've been there. Ben's been there.\par \par \uc2 Tomorrow on SPECIAL REPORT, our "Common Ground" segment, international edition, with three European defense ministers, their efforts to end the war in Ukraine all together.\par \par \uc2 Remember, if you can't catch us live, set your DVR, 6:00 p.m. in the east, 3:00 p.m. on the west coast. Somebody from Alabama said, you know, it's 5:00 p.m. where we are, so we will put that in there too. You can follow me on TikTok, \uc2 Instagram\uc2 , and X, @Bretbaier for exclusive behind the scenes content.\par \par \uc2 Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight and every night. That's it for this SPECIAL REPORT, fair, balanced, and unafraid. THE INGRAHAM ANGLE is now.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2025 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2025 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document FNSPBB0020250725el7o00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Booker & Padilla Support Illegals Over ICE; Dems Cry Out As Trump Enforces Immigration Laws; Trump Warns ICE Attacks Are Being Funded; Dems OK With Masks For Looters & Pro-\uc2 Hamas\uc2  Crowd; Voters Want Deportation, Dems Want More Illegals; \uc2 Microsoft\uc2  Lays Off U.S. Workers To Hire Foreigners; 