ne when looters wear masks to conceal their identities, pulling the Louis Vuitton off the shelves, and Democrats wouldn't think of passing laws banning face masks at any of the protests. Funny how masks were a First Amendment right for the BLM rioters, for the \uc2 Hamas\uc2  cheerleaders, and abolish ICE mobs, but suddenly dangerous when they're worn by people arresting child predators, individuals like Alvaro De Jesus Martinez-Juarez, convicted child sex predator, deported to Guatemala just last week, thank you, ICE, or this gem, Javier Zeledon Reyes, who admitted massacring 20 people in Nicaragua and he is linked to a Mexican cartel, now deported. These are the victims, victims that Democrats think deserve to see the faces of the agents that thankfully arrest them.\par \par \uc2 So, unmask ICE? How about we unmask the real motives of senators Padilla, Booker, and all their progressive pals? Their motives, to scare agents into silence and to hamstring law enforcement. Until Democrats get back into power, this is what they're hoping. They intimidate all the agents, they hurt recruiting of agents, and then once they get back into power, they'll fling open the border once again to more freeloaders, gang bangers, drug pushers and of course, just run-of-the-mill violent criminals.\par \par \uc2 But, here is my prediction tonight. As Democrats' true motives and all their obvious hypocrisy become clear, more Americans will turn to the America First movement, including legal immigrants, because it's the only sane option for our very survival, and that's The Angle.\par \par \uc2 With us now for his reaction to this insane bill being pushed by Democrats is Senator \uc2 Josh Hawley\uc2  from Missouri. Senator, you and I have talked about this. I mean, they want -- remember when they wanted those poor little toddlers on the planes with their bibs. They had to have the masks on. The kids were pulling them off. And Democrats are like, you mask up, little Johnny, but now, now they don't like masks when they're actually protecting the families of these ICE agents.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOSH HAWLEY\uc2  (R-MO): Yeah. I remember really well, Laura, because my kids were some of those toddlers on the planes, and I still remember being threatened with expulsion from the plane permanently, unless my kid, my three-year-old, my four-year-old, kept the mask on his face. I mean, these people wanted to solder the masks on our children permanently so you could never take them off. They have no problem with the Antifa losers wearing masks all the time on campuses and everywhere else. But, if you operating with the badge, oh, no, now you're enemy number one. You shouldn't be able to protect yourself and your family. It's exactly backwards, Laura.\par \par \uc2 We ought to say, when you have the badge on, you are operating to protect all of us. You represent all of us. You ought to get all of the protection that you can possibly have. If you're a looter or a rioter, you don't have any right to be anonymous. You ought to be prosecuted. As usual, Democrats are on the side of the criminals, not on the side of the American people.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, someone like a \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 , who has been reasonable in the past on some issues, I mean, he has had his moments, but you can actually have a conversation with \uc2 Cory Booker\uc2 . What is he thinking here, do you think? Because to me, this seems like political suicide for the Democrats. Most Americans want every single illegal out of this country. They don't want exceptions. They don't want a carve-out for hospitality or carve-outs for farm workers. Sorry. They want them all gone, bye, bye, and then you can reapply later, maybe. But, what's Booker thinking about here?\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: Yeah. I agree with everything. I agree with everything you just said, by the way, about what Americans want. I think that is 100 percent accurate. But, the Democrats, you got to remember, their base now, Laura, their base are increasingly illegals, criminals and people who love criminals. Look at the LA riots. The Democrats are out there cheering them on. Here you've got these rioters burning cars, blowing up stuff and what, waving the Mexican flag, and the Democrats are saying, oh, peaceful protests. This is wonderful. Keep it up.\par \par \uc2 I think they are so out of touch with the American people. They've become the party of crime and lawlessness. We're the party of law and order. They're the party of the criminals and the illegal elements, and that is who they represent. That's who votes for them. And you see them responding to it now. Again, it is exactly backward, totally upside down.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, and I think Americans watching tonight are shocked to learn that this group, CHIRLA, the Committee for Humane Immigrant Rights, I'm probably botching it, but that basically captures it, that at one point they received $34 million in federal grant money. Now, they're all over the protests, government grant money, but they're all over these protests. They support the protests and so forth. Some of them have turned violent. I'm not trying to make a direct connection here. But, why are these groups getting so much money, and why is that a good use of taxpayer dollars, whether it's state, local or federal?\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: They're getting so much money because the Democrats have turned the nonprofit world and these government grants into a huge money laundering operation, that's why, and that's why the work that the Trump administration has done on exposing \uc2 USAID\uc2 , all of these other nonprofits that are taking taxpayer money, laundering it through into, frankly, illegal activities, as we're seeing with these riots.\par \par \uc2 It's also why, Laura, we need to follow that money for all of these rioters, for all of this civil unrest that's going on. I mean, it's really not even civil. It's criminal unrest that's going on. We need to know who is funding it, where is it coming from. There is nothing that the Department of Justice is doing right now that is more important than getting a read on this money, finding out who is using it, who is pouring it in to all of these illegal groups, and we've got to stop the government funding of all of it. Turn off the money spigots.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, there is an online fundraiser, Senator, that is purportedly being used to raise funds for the 10 arrested ICE attackers in Texas. Now, it only has about nine grand in it so far, but the description of this fundraiser says, those currently face serious charges aimed not only at ruining their lives, but signaling an authoritarian criminalization of dissent and protest against ICE. Now, this is one account on GiveSendGo. But, what does this tell you about where the mindset is of some of these rabid ideologues in the Democrat Party?\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: That tells me it's been completely overtaken by a bunch of Marxist gobbledygook. I mean, what you just read there and shown on screen is absurd. I mean, anybody with a brain who looks at that, it's like, are you kidding me? But, once again, today's Democrat Party has been captured by these loonies. I mean, they've really become the party of the mentally unstable lunatics, and this is why it is absolutely vital we get back to law and order.\par \par \uc2 What the President is doing here is just the right thing, whether it was calling out the guard in LA, whether it's protecting those who wear the badge now, turning off the money from all of these nonprofits who are laundering it, turning off the taxpayer funding. We've got to put a stop to all of this. This is the time to root out the rot, expose it, tear it out of our government, tear it out of our system, and expose these people for the criminals that they are.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And at the same time, Senator, we have American corporations that are firing American workers and seemingly replacing them with