ritarian and trying to apply these jihadi values.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well -- and I agree with you, this idea that we should just abandon the cities and say, Oh, they should all collapse. That's not what America First is. These are great American cities. Why should we have that attitude? I think we should go all in and sell the America First agenda and prosperity and peace and law and order and our wonderful history. I think that's the winning message.\par \par \uc2 LONSDALE: One of my big goals is to get the red state governors to step up and fight for our cities and show that our civilization can take these things back and stop them from funding all this commie nonsense. So, let's do it.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: All right. Joe, great to talk to you, as always. Good to see you.\par \par \uc2 And up next, conservatives livid over the Epstein client list. But, will a lawsuit actually give us answers? Coming up.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: We were underage. We were little girls. I started going to him when I was like 14, 15. By the time I was 16, I brought him up to 75 girls. All the ages of, you know, 14, 15, 16. School parties is where I'd recruit him from. All Jeffrey cared about was go find me more girls. His appetite was insatiable. He couldn't stop.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Well, yesterday, President Trump and his A.G. hoped that they had put an end to the Epstein story.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2 , PRESIDENT OF THE UNITED STATES OF AMERICA: I can't believe you're asking a question on Epstein at a time like this where we're having some of the greatest success, and also tragedy with what happened in Texas. It just seems like a desecration.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I said -- I was asked a question about the client list, and my response was, it's sitting on my desk to be reviewed, meaning the file along with VJFK, MLK