ve open cabinet hearings. He invites people into the Oval Office to talk about the executive orders that he's signing. It's a running dialogue with the American people.\par \par \uc2 That's the best way you restore trust. But what the Biden administration did was destroy that trust and they're continuing that effort with a lot of minions around him and they're probably trying to protect their own reputations because they knew all along this guy wasn't competent.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, it certainly seems like there was some type of ongoing fraud upon the American people. Was it agreed upon? Was it an official thing, or was it an unofficial thing like, wink, wink, keep the old man in the pool area and don't let him come in right now? I mean, we don't know how it went down.\par \par \uc2 But we do know that powerful people were circling him and preventing others from getting into him, even senators complain that they couldn't get access to the president when they wanted. Now, the senator can't reach the president of the United States, can a cabinet secretary?\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: Right. Well, even members of his own party. I've talked to Democrats who just had no contact with them, and that was on purpose because he would sort of wander on, he would fall asleep, he lost his place in conversations, and I take no pleasure in this.\par \par \uc2 I mean, if you don't live long enough, you know, these things happen. But this guy is the president of the United States. And this fraud that was perpetrated on the American people, you know, can't go unchecked.\par \par \uc2 And you also -- it's also important to remember, the people who were actually in charged then were these radicals who were writing white papers on open borders. They actually did it. They allowed 20 million people in here while \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  was asleep at the switch, quite literally.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, real world consequences to the ongoing fraud. Senator, as always, thank you so muc