ngerously close to normalizing behavior like that.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: So, end of democracy still the message?\par \par \uc2 FLEISCHER: So out of touch. You know what? End democracy is shooting \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but ends democracy is removing \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's name from the ballot in Colorado and Illinois and in Maine as the Democrats sought to do. Those are the types of things that are threats to democracy.\par \par \uc2 What's a threat to democracies in the state of Maine, removing the vote from a legislator who stood up to prevent boys from competing against girls in sports, and the majority Democrat legislature said you can no longer vote or speak on the floor as a result of that stance you took. These are the threats to the democracy.\par \par \uc2 But back to the campaign, back to the midterm especially, Kayleigh, the biggest factor is going to be \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's approval rating. It was minus 18 in 2022, and it was -- I'm sorry. In 2018 when Republicans lost the House, it's only minus five now. If Trump is popular, Republicans are in much better shape.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Yep. And you pass that big beautiful bill. No tax on tips. No tax on overtime. And I think you're going to see that soar. Thank you very much, Ari. Talk to you soon.\par \par \uc2 FLEISCHER: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 MCENANY: Well, the left will stop at nothing to try to get Trump. Case in point, the Biden DOJ. I could not believe this. Listen to this. These are internal \uc2 FBI\uc2  emails. They were obtained by Senator \uc2 Chuck Grassley\uc2 , and they revealed that rogue agents and prosecutors were looking for ways to pile on new criminal charges against the president over January 6.\par \par \uc2 Well, this time it was over his involvement with the J6 prisoner choir. Here with the details is Miranda Devine, New York Post columnist and Fox News contributor. Miranda, these emails are stunning, and I want to read to you part of one 