ack \uc2 Obama\uc2 !\par \par \uc2 (CHEERING)\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH: This week former president \uc2 Obama\uc2  reemerged, telling a Connecticut crowd progressives must stay in the fight.\par \par \uc2 BARACK OBAMA\uc2 , FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT: We are going to have to then decide what our commitments are. It will be uncomfortable for a time.\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH: New York City mayoral candidate Brad Lander seemed to want to pick a fight over immigration as he was arrested this week for allegedly assaulting law enforcement officers who were trying to detain a migrant. So far no charges have been filed.\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 ALEX PADILLA\uc2 , (D-CA): I have questions for the secretary.\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH: The incident coming a week after California Senator \uc2 Alex Padilla\uc2  was detained for interrupting Homeland Security Secretary \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 's news conference in Los Angeles.\par \par \uc2 Senator Padilla and other Democrats quickly moved to fundraise off the moment.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO TAPE)\par \par \uc2 MEREDITH (on camera): Vermont Senator \uc2 Bernie Sanders\uc2  is also urging Democrats to speak out. This weekend he's touring the south, making stops in Louisiana, Texas, and Oklahoma, encouraging voters to revolt against the Trump administration. Bret?\par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS ANCHOR: Mark, thank you.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, many people around the country are celebrating Juneteenth, commemorating the emancipation of slaves across the U.S. Cities across the country are holding events. former president \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is attending a church at a historic church in Galveston. It is one of the locations where the order ending slavery in Texas was read on this date in 1865, two years after President \uc2 Abraham Lincoln\uc2  issued the emancipation proclamation.\par \par \uc2 Religion correspondent Lauren Green is in Times Square tonight with the story. Good evening, Lauren.\par \par \uc2 LAUREN GREEN, FOX NEWS RELIGION CORRESP