t's all that rained down were these assigned -- what he said was racist, what he said was xenophobic. And then you go, well, no, actually that's your interpretation if you're reading his mind. And I found myself guilty of that. And that was the biggest lesson for me and for the future.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: Well, Kennedy, we're going to let you deal with this tomorrow or a little later in the show here. Oh, go.\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY MONTGOMERY: I will say this. A lot of people thought they were disqualifying comments when he ascended down the golden escalator. That was just an Amuse-bouche.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: "ONE MORE THING" is up next. "ONE MORE THING" --\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 PERINO: It's time now for "ONE MORE THING." Greg?\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: Oh, we got a great show tonight. We got the return of Kat Tipmf after months of being out.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: Hear! Hear! Welcome back, Kat.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: David Angelo, Kennedy, and Tyrus. Tune in 10:00 p.m.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Jesse?\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: All right, so the twins graduated from 8th grade. I'm so proud of them. Ellie won the math award. Sophia spoke at graduation and won the spirit award. Very, very proud.\par \par \uc2 Tonight, Pete Hegseth and Karoline Leavitt at 8:00. And Johnny was at the military parade.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: We're not playing that. OK. Perino on Politics with Matt Whitlock on -- is up now. And Harold.\par \par \uc2 FORD JR.: Congrats to J. J. Spaun for winning the U.S. Open what. What a finish. Congrats to his family.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: I saw that putt.\par \par \uc2 WATTERS: That was great. What a way to win.\par \par \uc2 GUTFELD: We're doing this?\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Kennedy?\par \par \uc2 KENNEDY MONTGOMERY: Summer of Chaos: Inside Seattle's CHOP Zone on Fox Nation. Subscribe now.\par \par \uc2 PERINO: Oh, yes. I want them all that chop jazz. That's it for us. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and P