rademark, copyright or other notice from copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 EMILY COMPAGNO, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONTRIBUTOR: All right, guys. That's it for us. Have a great night.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. ALEX PADILLA (D-CA): I'm Senator \uc2 Alex Padilla\uc2 . I have question for the secretary. Because the fact of the matter is, a half a dozen violent criminals that you're rotating on your -- on your --\par \par \uc2 KRISTI NOEM, UNITED STATES SECRETARY OF HOMELAND SECURITY: I also want to talk on --\par \par \uc2 PADILLA: Hands off!\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: On the ground. On the ground. On the ground.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 AISHAH HASNIE, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONGRESSIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Tensions over immigration raids and violent protests boiling over in Los Angeles as a sitting U.S. senator there on your screen, confronts a member of the president's Cabinet, and then, is forcibly removed and placed into handcuffs.\par \par \uc2 Fox News was there in the room as it all went down.\par \par \uc2 Good evening to you. Welcome to Washington. I'm Aishah Hasnie, in for Bret Baier tonight.\par \par \uc2 And breaking tonight, California Democratic senator \uc2 Alex Padilla\uc2  says he was conducting his oversight duties when he was interrupted -- when he interrupted a news briefing by the Homeland Security secretary about the Los Angeles riots.\par \par \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  says Padilla did not identify himself and that no one knew who he was when Secret Service jumped in.\par \par \uc2 Bill Melugin was there for it all. He shot video of the incident. He joins us in a few moments here.\par \par \uc2 Meanwhile, congressional Democrats are enraged. Chad Pergram will take us inside a heated Capitol Hill tonight.\par \par \uc2 Also, anti-ICE protests are spreading to many other cities across the nation. And Steve Harrigan is in L.A.\par \par \uc2 Peter Doocy is at the White House for us, as President Trump searches for answers on who is funding these protests.\par \par \uc2 But we begin tonight at the center of the storm. The physical confrontation involving Senator Padilla. It happened right in front of correspondent Bill Melugin, and he is here to tell us what happened.\par \par \uc2 Good evening, Bill.\par \par \uc2 BILL MELUGIN, FOX NEWS CHANNEL NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Yes, Aishah, good evening to you.\par \par \uc2 DHS Secretary \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2  had been giving a press conference for just a few minutes or so, when I heard somebody to my right yell out to her and interrupt her.\par \par \uc2 I initially thought it was just a protester. Then, I saw security grab that person, turn him around and push him back. That's when I realized, oh, wow, OK, this is Senator \uc2 Alex Padilla\uc2 . I pulled out my phone and shot this video.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 PADILLA: I am Senator \uc2 Alex Padilla\uc2 . I have question for the secretary. Because the fact of the matter is, a half a dozen --\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN (voice over): So, you can see, Secret Service agents getting physical with Senator Padilla. There was some pushing and shoving both ways. The senator yelled out, I'm Senator \uc2 Alex Padilla\uc2 . They ultimately forcibly removed him from the room, but things continued out in the hallway. Take a look at this. Padilla staffers posted their own video of him being taken down to the ground by these agents.\par \par \uc2 He was temporarily handcuffed before ultimately being released. Senator Padilla then, held a press conference outside the building just a short time later.\par \par \uc2 PADILLA: If this is how the \uc2 Department of Homeland Security\uc2  responds to a senator with a question, you can only imagine what they are doing to farm workers, to cooks, to day laborers out in the Los Angeles community, and throughout California, and throughout the country.\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN (voice over): Now, after the incident, Secretary Noem told us, she had a 10 to 15-minute meeting with Senator Padilla, which she described as cordial and beneficial. She told us they exchanged phone numbers and opened up a line of communication.\par \par \uc2 NOEM: He and I are probably not going to agree on probably 90 percent of things. But we both had left that room, recognizing that if we have civil conversations, that we'll get to better results. And there was a few things in there we agreed on, and I informed him on the president's opinion and the president's executive authorities that he's exercising.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 MELUGIN: And the \uc2 FBI\uc2  here in L.A. put out a statement that saying, Senator Padilla was not wearing his Senate security pin. They say he was being disruptive. But that as soon as he was positively identified, he was released from custody. We'll send it back to you.\par \par \uc2 HASNIE: Bill Melugin, live for us right there on the scene in Los Angeles. Thank you, Bill.\par \par \uc2 Well, some of the words Democrats are using tonight about the Padilla incident includes revolting, repugnant, abhorrent, and outrageous.\par \par \uc2 Let's get some more color tonight from senior congressional correspondent Chad Pergram. He is on Capitol Hill. Good evening to you, Chad.\par \par \uc2 CHAD PERGRAM, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CONGRESSIONAL CORRESPONDENT: Aishah, good evening.\par \par \uc2 The video of Padilla, inflamed Capitol Hill. Senate Democrats rushed to the floor to defend their colleague.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 CHUCK SCHUMER\uc2  (D-NY): Senator Padilla was exercising his duty as a Senator for his constituents to try and find out what happened. And instead, he gets manhandled, thrown out of the room, thrown out of down on the ground and handcuffed.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): Democrats barged into GOP leadership offices, demanding an investigation and scolding the brass.\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 ADRIANO ESPAILLAT\uc2  (D-NY): Both the Speaker and Leader Thune should step up to the moment and preserve the institutions of Congress, which are a balance in democracy, an important balance in democracy.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): The fracas sparked a nasty shouting match at a House hearing for sanctuary cities.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: No, you commit on the record.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Thank you.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Subpoenaing \uc2 Kristi Noem\uc2 , because a U.S. senator was just thrown to the ground and detained in his own --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Hey, listen, listen, listen.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Democrats can't follow the rules, can't follow the law. Cannot follow the rules.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: You are out of order.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Will you just shut up? Just shot up.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Will you --\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (voice over): House Speaker Mike Johnson said Padilla's conduct was, "wildly inappropriate" and beneath a lawmaker. And since Democrats' Hector Johnson, as he tried to speak with the press.\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE JOHNSON (R-LA): My view is it was wildly inappropriate.\par \par \uc2 You don't charge a sitting Cabinet secretary, and everybody can draw their own conclusions.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It's a lie! A lie!\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: You can see it's a heated debate here.\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM: Can you respond to some of this people heckling you here, Mr. Speaker?\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: I'm not going to respond to that. Look, let me just --\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Do you support an investigation --\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: Hold on. Wait just a second.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Do you think there is -- investigation into what happen?\par \par \uc2 JOHNSON: I think the American people can draw their own conclusions.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 PERGRAM (on camera): Now, Johnson believes Padilla earned a censure.\par