then we were assured by people around him that he was just exhausted.\par \par \uc2 I remember feeling, I want to talk about this as a huge liability. I want to talk about this as something \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  can overcome. But I'm not going to go so far as to say, I think \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  must drop out. He is too old to be president.\par \par \uc2 A, because I didn't know exactly what was going on behind the scenes. But, B, if \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  is the candidate, I want him to (BLEEP) win because I care about the country.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BOOTHE: Joining me now is Jason Rantz, Seattle radio host, and Terry Schilling, American Principles Project President. Jason, you watch that clip. What are they not willing to lie about?\par \par \uc2 JASON RANTZ, SEATTLE RADIO HOST: I love the branding move. You should listen to me on a podcast because I'm going to totally lie to you, because I think it might benefit my career in the country, which of course it doesn't benefit anything other than maybe his access to the White House.\par \par \uc2 These are folks who not only lied so that Biden could win, but it's important to understand they're lying about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  so he loses. This is what they're about. They will say and do anything if it satisfies some sort of political agenda of theirs.\par \par \uc2 BOOTHE: Well, and what else are they lying about? Terry, so David Hogg, the soon to be out of a job DNC vice chair, thinks he has his finger on the pulse of what the Democratic Party needs. Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Jasmine Crockett, I love her. She is amazing.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Yeah.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I think that people want to see somebody who fights and calls out (BLEEP) ultimately. I think that's what Jasmine does, and we need a hell of a lot more people that are out there that are willing to do just that.\par \par \uc2 And call people out on their B.S. and not say, oh my god, the Republicans are going to criticize me for saying this. Screw that. They're going to criticize you no matter what. So, what we should be asking ourselves is what are we really fighting for?\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BOOTHE: Terry, is David Hogg a Republican plant? I love his advice.\par \par \uc2 TERRY SCHILLING, PRESIDENT, AMERICAN PRINCIPLES PROJECT: Lisa, we need to make this guy the chairman of the DNC. I mean, I hate that they're removing him. He's an absolute genius. He's an absolute madman. Let's get him in charge of the entire party. It will be the best thing ever for Republicans.\par \par \uc2 No. Listen. This is a joke. Jasmine Crockett is a joke. She's fundamentally unserious. She's fake. She's astroturf. But, look, the Democrats are an obvious mess, and we -- the Republicans should just step back and let them implode.\par \par \uc2 BOOTHE: Jason, so Chicago Mayor Brandon Johnson is bragging about how he makes his hiring decisions. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: There's some detractors that will push back on me and say, you know, the only thing that mayor talk -- the mayor talks about is the hiring of black people. No. What I'm saying is when you hire our people, we always look out for everybody else. We are the most generous people on the planet.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 BOOTHE: He's now under investigation by the DOJ over those hiring practices. Jason, you've got about a minute here. Your reaction to that?\par \par \uc2 RANTZ: I mean, I will say this. Brandon Johnson generously espouses racism and incompetence. I suppose you can make that claim. This is 2025, and we have to remind people that you're not supposed to choose folks on the basis of their skin color and create these massive generalizations of what you think they are capable of doing and how you think they're going to act.\par \par \uc2 I thought we all established this as racist, but in Chicago where he continues to push