al security issues here are paramount. We cannot rely on Communist China for our prescription drugs. We cannot rely on Taiwan for our advanced semiconductor chips.\par \par \uc2 This is the beginning of the United States becoming independent for the things that we need. This is brilliant. President Trump knows this, and that's why he's putting this in place. Markets are selling off right now, Laura, and I will tell you --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Good time to buy.\par \par \uc2 BARTIROMO: -- once we get a nice sell-off tomorrow, I would be buying this market with both hands.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, Maria, as always, so awesome to have you on. Thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 BARTIROMO: Thanks, Laura.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And just ahead, it's time for Republicans to get tough. Yes, get tough with some common sense. The Democrats fear and smear campaign, one win, but other losses. We'll talk about it next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Republicans saw big wins in the special election last night, both Florida House seats stayed red despite those projections you were hearing and excellent news in Wisconsin, where voter ID is now enshrined in the state constitution there. But of course, it wasn't all good. Democrat Susan Crawford handily won that important Wisconsin Supreme Court race, which could give two more seats to the Democrats with redistricting and the Democrat Party, of course, is salivating.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 REP. \uc2 MARK POCAN\uc2  (D-WI): People don't want their health care and long-term care cut. They don't want education cut. They don't want food assistance cut. Also that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  and \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  can get a tax cut.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: They are causing disruption. They are causing chaos.\par \par \uc2 SCHUMER: Americans are tired of the chaos. They are tired of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  attacking Social Security, Medicaid, Medicare.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMA