e a number of Republicans who simply refuse to do that. And I know you don't want to call out your colleagues. I know that's not the senatorial way. But I do think there is a huge disconnect here. If it's so urgent that you push the president's agenda through, and stop these nationwide injunctions, then you have to stay in session to move these votes forward, just the senate rules.\par \par \uc2 So, when you're out of session, I mean, you get some recess appointments in, but you can't get the agenda through. So, what's your message to your colleagues on both sides of the aisle tonight about getting this done?\par \par \uc2 SCHMITT: Well, I think it's imperative. I think that the president won a mandate from the American people, not just all the battleground states, but the popular vote. And he ran on a message of disrupting permanent Washington.\par \par \uc2 What you're seeing now is sort of the -- at the Rose Garden with the announcement of actually putting America First, these policies, you're seeing the last dying gasp of permanent Washington pushing back and resisting an agenda the American people want.\par \par \uc2 We should work as hard as we possibly can to actually get that done. I know I'm here for it and I hope a lot of other people are too.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Senator, you're always diplomatic, much more so than I am. Thank you so much for joining us tonight.\par \par \uc2 All right. Jasmine Crockett lashes out. Well, what else is new? And Alec Baldwin is preparing for war? Seen and Unseen, Raymond Arroyo has it and it's next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It is time for Seen and Unseen where we reveal the stories behind the headlines. For that, we turn to Fox News contributor, Raymond Arroyo. All right, Raymond. Your favorite, Jasmine Crockett said that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  should be taken down. Now, she was warned by Pam Bondi to tread carefully, but Jasmine didn't like that.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2