he snitches that are alerting the illegal aliens and the gang members to the raids, what can be done there, anything?\par \par \uc2 WOLF: Well, absolutely. You can hold them accountable as well. So, you can investigate. And if you find them, you've got to prosecute them. And it's not just irresponsible what they're doing. It's criminal what they're doing because it's putting officers, law enforcement officers' lives in danger if you're tipping off the bad folks as they come in and to do an operation.\par \par \uc2 So, that is also about accountability. Again, I think it sends a strong signal if you can identify and then prosecute.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, make them pay for that. Chad, as always, thank you. All right, we come back. A rap battle extraordinaire. \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  versus \uc2 Sam Altman\uc2 . Failla, next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now it's time for WTF, What the Failla? Joining me now, Jimmy Failla, host of Fox News Saturday night. All right, Jimmy, we're watching the battle of the billionaires unfold. OK, so this investors group backed by \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  is trying to buy open AI from CEO \uc2 Sam Altman\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Open AI is not for sale. The open admission is not for sale. Elon tries all sorts of things for a long time.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Do you think Musk's approach then is from a position of insecurity about XAI?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Probably his whole life is from a position of insecurity, I feel for the guy.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: You feel for him?\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I do, actually. I don't think he's like a happy person, I do feel for him.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Seem pretty happy today, Jimmy. I don't know. He seems pretty happy with his son, like, giving us a tutorial in the Oval. He was very happy.\par \par \uc2 JIMMY FAILLA, FOX NEWS SATURDAY HOST: Yeah, to be fair, I mean, let's be honest. If you look at \uc2