ue of alcohol?\par \par \uc2 HEGSETH: No, we've had great conversations about who I am and what I believe, and, frankly, the man I am today because of my faith in my Lord and Savior, Jesus Christ, and my incredible wife, Jenny right here. I'm a different man than I was years ago. And that's a redemption story that I think a lot of Americans appreciate.\par \par \uc2 And I know from fellow vets that I've spent time with, they resonate with that as well. You fight, you go do tough things in tough places on behalf of your country. And sometimes that changes you a little bit. And by the grace of God and my Lord and Savior, I had an opportunity to come on up out of it and do great things with great veterans organizations that fought for vets, that fought for reform at the V.A. and for war fighters and at the Fox News Channel to advocate for those very same causes.\par \par \uc2 And I'm proud of what I fought for. I'm not going to back down from them one bit. I will answer all of these senators' questions, but this will not be a process tried in the media. I don't answer to anyone in this group, none of you, not to that camera at all. I answer to President Trump, who received 76 million votes on behalf and a mandate for change. I answer to the 50 -- the 100 senators who are part of this process and those in the committee. And I answer to my Lord and Savior, and my wife and my family. I'm proud to be here. And as long as \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  wants me in this fight, I'm going to be standing right here in this fight, fighting to bring our Pentagon back to what it needs to be.\par \par \uc2 REPORTER: What have your conversations been --\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 MACCALLUM: Peter Hegseth, our colleague here for many years, saying that he is standing firm, that he has the support of President Trump, who nominated him and that he has had a good week on Capitol Hill and that he will try to earn the support of every one of those senators who will be holding tho