-elect \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  -- next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: All right, airline executives grilled on Capitol Hill today about all these secret fees and how it started getting billions of dollars from, well, seat assignments -- after this.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 CAVUTO: You know, it almost has a look at the drone invasion going on in New Jersey, but when it involves the New Jersey home of the president- elected United States, it does catch more attention than normal, even though this has been running rampant for weeks now throughout much of the Garden State.\par \par \uc2 Nate Foy has more from Morristown, New Jersey.\par \par \uc2 Hey, Nate.\par \par \uc2 FOY: Hey, Neil.\par \par \uc2 So, just within the past couple of hours, local authorities put out an additional statement reiterating that there is no threat to public safety because of these drones. But we're speaking with witnesses who are concerned because, as you mentioned, they're flying near sensitive areas.\par \par \uc2 But also, just in general, these drones, we're told, are bigger than drones you would typically see people flying for fun. In fact, one witness said they looked like commercial military drones. Here's another witness describing what they look like.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: This one is extremely low. It's loud. And it's really huge.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: It's so big. It looks so much closer in person.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Yes, my camera doesn't do it. It looks like a spaceship.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 FOY: So now the \uc2 FBI\uc2  is investigating, with state and local authorities saying -- quote -- "Witnesses have spotted the cluster of what look to be drones and a possible fixed-wing aircraft."\par \par \uc2 A witness tells FOX that he and his neighbors are confused and worried about where these drones are coming from. He said he lives about a 