y tickets for Jimmy's Night of Comedy on foxnation.com. All right, that's it for us tonight. Make sure to follow me on social media. And speaking of that, a lot of you are asking for photos from the Texas, Texas A&M game that I was at over the weekend with my kids, my daughter goes there. And here it is.\par \par \uc2 So, this is what we look like. And it was before the loss, OK? We're in a very good mood at that point. We're in such a good mood afterward. All right, but Alabama might make the playoffs. All right, Jesse Watters and the gang, they take it all from here.\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020241204ekc300001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Jack Smith Led The Witch Hunt Against \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ; DOJ Raided Mar- A-Lago To Embarrass \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 ; Democrats never learn from their mistakes; What's next for \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2 ; Democrats only cried over migrant children under Trump; Where are the liberal tears over the border now; Trump reveals what he'll do on day one; Venezuela gang recruiting migrant children in New York City; Biden bumbles through annual White House Turkey pardon; Biden hosts dinner to thank allies and White House staff, as \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  misses Biden's gratitude dinner; A fattening course, University of Maryland offers class on fat studies\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Laura Ingraham, Mollie Hemingway, Mary Katharine Ham,  Laura Ingraham, Raymond Arroyo \par \uc2 7,778 \uc2 words\par \uc2 25 November 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 VIQ Solutions, Inc. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: -- handcrafted ornaments from Alaska. Good stuff. It's the season. Tomorrow on Special Report, we'll take you to Texas and the incoming border czar Tom Homan tours the southern border with Governor Greg Abbott. We'll do it, fair, balanced and still unafraid. Here's Laura.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. Just moments ago, on Truth Social, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  revealed one of his first acts as President. This is a big one. On January 20th, as one of his many first executive orders, he will sign all necessary documents to charge Mexico and Canada a 25 percent tariff on all products coming into the United States and it's ridiculous, open borders. It's time for them to pay a very big price. Most of that, of course, focus on Mexico there, more on that later. Plus, \uc2 Eric Trump\uc2  will react to that and a lot more. But first, lawfare loses. That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 Well, he came in very hot against Trump.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JACK SMITH, ATTORNEY: Good evening. Today, an indictment was unsealed charging \uc2 Donald J. Trump\uc2  with conspiring to defraud the United States, conspiring to disenfranchise voters, and conspiring and attempting to obstruct an official proceeding. The attack on our nation's capital on January 6, 2021, was an unprecedented assault on the seat of American democracy.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: So, sanctimonious, but it turns out, the unprecedented assault on our democracy was committed not by \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 , but by the legal henchmen like Jack Smith and their political and media backers.\par \par \uc2 Now today, Smith was compelled to file motions to dismiss his cases against Trump, one of which was promptly granted by D.C. District Judge \uc2 Tanya Chutkan\uc2 . Now, this is obviously a huge victory for President-elect Trump, but Smith and his allies tried their best to frame the result as not based on the merits, but simply compelled by long-standing policy.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 EVAN PEREZ, CNN SENIOR JUSTICE CORRESPONDENT: This has nothing to do with the strength of the case. This simply has to do with the verdict, essentially that voters gave on the Justice Department policy, long- standing Justice Department policy, the Department is not allowed to prosecute a president, a sitting president that shield essentially also applies to him as an elected President, as the President-elect.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, when the news came out, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  posted on Truth Social that the cases were empty and lawless and should never have been brought.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KRISTEN HOLMES, CNN NATIONAL CORRESPONDENT: They are celebrating. This was the goal all along was that they would get these cases dropped. The idea of it actually being revived in their mind seems highly unlikely. This seems like the end of all this.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, but not so fast. While we love seeing these cases falling into the abyss, one after the other, the petty and vindictive Jack Smith made sure to request that the cases be dismissed without prejudice, meaning?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: These cases could be revived after Trump serves this next term, right?\par \par \uc2 PEREZ: That's right. I mean, look, if you look at the language that the Special Counsel used, and that the judge uses in deciding this without prejudice, means that when \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is no longer President of the United States, these cases could be revived.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yes, theoretically, the charges could be reinstated