e've got to make it from now to then. And this policy is a disaster.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, a friend of mine described it as it's almost like Biden or whoever is making this call, and you wonder who is, is mining the political and military landscape to cause trouble for Trump. However, he just met with Trump. Is there any possibility that he and Trump talked about this?\par \par \uc2 Not that Trump would be in favor of this, but it's kind of a chess move to get Putin to the table, or do you think that's just probably not likely?\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: Well, it looks like escalation to me, Laura. It looks like a green light for escalation on the part of Ukraine. And then Russia, as you pointed out, what would happen if Russia would launch and retaliate missiles into the territory of a \uc2 NATO\uc2  member? Then our treaty obligations would be triggered. Then we're talking about a full-scale war.\par \par \uc2 I can't imagine that President Trump wants that. He's been totally against it. What I'm sure he wants is for Biden to stop screwing this up and allow him to get into office and begin to work towards America's security interest.\par \par \uc2 Let's remember what our interests in the region are. It's our national security. That's what we ought to be putting first. And giving a green light to shoot missiles into Russia, that's not putting our interests first. It's putting them last.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's insane. Do you think Biden made this call? Is he the one who came up with this idea?\par \par \uc2 HAWLEY: I don't think Biden's making any calls. I think it's other people within the deep state who want this conflict to go on forever. This is escalation. And I think that's what's going on here.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, trying to prevent Trump from actually being able to pull out of the situation. That's what they did in Afghanistan to him. Senator, as always, thank you so much.\par \par \uc2 And up next, D.C. bureaucrats are freaking out tonight