 or he didn't get a Reaganist or Nixonian electoral college. But you look at the issues, Laura. Every one of those issues was a mandate.\par \par \uc2 Sixty-five percent close the border. Sixty-five percent shrink government. Change the foreign policy. Reduce crime. Hyperinflation. He's riding a crest of issues that are even polling more popular than the vote that he's does. So, he does have a mandate.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: An MSNBC guest, Victor, is trashing DOGE's plans. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: This isn't about adherence to the Constitution. This isn't about rule of law. This isn't about reforming, you know, bureaucracies that need, you know, a couple of nuances here and there to make them more efficient. This is about destroying our current government in its form.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Victor, we're destroying government in its form.\par \par \uc2 HANSON: I guess she thinks that the Department of Education and the Department of Energy are somewhere in the Constitution. They're not. They're pretty late additions. A lot of these programs, entities, agencies weren't even in existence until the modern period.\par \par \uc2 And everybody understands that except the people who cling to them. They know what's coming and they don't know what to do with it, so they're in a panic mode.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, I think a COVID, Victor, gave people license to kind of sit around in their sweatpants and t-shirts and zoom into work, usually turning the video part off. And then they're going off to Hawaii, and they're going to different places. And like, I'm just as efficient.\par \par \uc2 But if you're an essential-personnel, some essential worker, and you don't show up for during a snowstorm, you lose your essential worker status pretty quick. So maybe that's a good way to cut staffing. If you don't show up, then you're not essential.\par \par \uc2 HANSON: Yeah, I think, they think they're in the academic world where there are such rules that they follow, but they're not. I think the best thing they could do, Laura, was go look at \uc2 Twitter\uc2  and ask if \uc2 Twitter\uc2  collapsed after Elon captured hundreds of superfluous employees. I don't think it did. It thrived.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That made it much, much more efficient. Victor, as always, thank you. All right, Joe and Mika's diplomatic mission goes sideways, while Biden gets totally lost. Raymond Arroyo has it all. Seen and Unseen is next.\par \par \uc2 (COMMERCIAL BREAK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's time for Seen and Unseen where we reveal the stories behind the headlines, and for that we turn to Fox News contributor, Raymond Arroyo. All right, Ray, as I alluded to the Angle, Scarborough and Brzezinski have returned from a diplomatic mission.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Joe and I went to Mar-a-Lago. It was the first time we have seen him in seven years.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: We didn't see eye to eye on a lot of issues, and we told him so.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: What we did agree on was to restart communications. My father often spoke with world leaders, with whom he and the United States profoundly disagreed.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 RAYMOND ARROYO, FOX NEWS CONTRIBUTOR: Laura, her father was a national security adviser to \uc2 Jimmy Carter\uc2 . Did I miss something here? When did Joe and Mika become the ambassadors to Mar-a-Lago? I didn't realize the Democratic Party appointed diplomats in defeat.\par \par \uc2 And by the way, this is not an overture to unity. This is an attempt to book a weekend show at NewsNation as their MSNBC morning show dies in the ratings. But did they think people would forget what they said about Trump just days ago?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: It's clear the president is stunningly ignorant. Probably the most ignorant president we will ever have.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: No, no, we can talk about Nazi, Germany, and I do it, I do it without any concerns whatsoever. And if people can't start drawing the parallels, well, you're just stupid.\par \par \uc2 If you believe in American capitalism, you should be worried about \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  being elected.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, just -- some of those clips went back to 2018. But right before the election, he was an insurrectionist, he was an election denier, he was fascistic. I mean, he was mentally deranged. I mean, but I guess winning has -- winning has benefits, Raymond. And you know.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: You call the guy a Nazi, one day, and ask for a season pass to his club the next --\par \par \uc2 (CROSSTALK)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I mean, what does that tell you about what they -- they never believed their own words. They never believed it. Otherwise, why are you having -- going to have a new segment, Coffee with Hitler? What is that? I don't understand that.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: High bowls with Hitler.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: No, no, no. Comedians and cabs, what is that? Comedians and whatever. It was like, Coffee with Hitler. All right, Raymond, the Scarborough's colleagues at MSNBC, apparently, and the gals at The View, did not take this diplomatic mission too kindly.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I don't think you need to sit down for 90 minutes at Mar-a-Lago and kiss his ring to be able to speak truth. So maybe they're not journalists in the true sense.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Oh, but she is.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Forgive us.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I'm sticking up for Joe and Mika now.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah, forgive us Edward R. Hostin, you know. Look, but that kind of thinking, to try to continue this narrative and defeat, Laura, this is why the Democratic Party lost. To have no self-reflection at this point seems very defeating. I mean, this has been, the country rejected this narrative just for the record.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, but it's pretty smart.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Meanwhile, other parts --\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's pretty smart. Hold on, Raymond. It's pretty smart of them. I mean, if you're them, if you're Joe and Mika, it's really their only card to play. What are they going to keep doing? Skating in the wind about Hitler?\par \par \uc2 That didn't work and they kind of admitted that and said, what we were doing didn't really work. We haven't changed our views, but we're going to try a different approach and we're going to talk to him. But it's really an act.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Somebody should tell Whoopi and the girls.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah, it was an act of survival, though. I think it's like survival of the fittest kind of move. But, go ahead.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Meanwhile, other parts of the Democratic Party, Laura, are in full meltdown. \uc2 The New York Times\uc2  featured a piece this weekend with the headline, Men? Maybe Not. Did you see that?\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I missed that, Jim. Well, I saw the piece that, I love this headline though, disappointed by the defeat of another female nominee, particularly young women online are channeling their disappointment into anger toward men as a whole. Oh, great.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Yeah, what a wonderful way to get a female elected in the future, Laura. I hate you. I won't have sex with you. I don't want to date you. They call it hetero-pessimism. I call it a recipe for extinction. I mean, this is the dumbest thing ever.\par \par \uc2 But the good news is, they're not having indiscriminate sex, so that clears up all those abortion rights questions that everybody was so worried about. No sex, no abortions. They took care of that pretty good.\par \par \uc2 And you know, Laura, I'm always looking for a cultural thread. There is a type of response underway. Apparently, runway models are now taking to the catwalk, not those people that you see there. But actual runway models in New York and Paris are proudly pregnant, and there's nothing better or more beautiful than a mama or a mama-to-be. So that's kind of a new trend here.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I think that's good. So, on the one hand they're there. So, they're celebrating having children, which I think it's -- didn't they go after that butcher guy for basically celebrating having children?\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: Right.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Kicker, your friend. I think they went out there -- yeah.\par \par \uc2 ARROYO: And you know, while that catwalk going on, Biden was at the G20 today, Laura. He missed the group photo, which gives you a sign of American's dominance in the world these days. He was off in the wing somewhere. Missed the photo.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: He was reaching. He was looking for his own new diplomatic mission, Raymond. All right, that's for us tonight. Jesse is next. See you tomorrow night.\par \par \uc2 END\par \par \uc2 Content and Programming Copyright 2024 Fox News Network, LLC. ALL  RIGHTS RESERVED. Copyright 2024 VIQ Media Transcription, Inc.  All  materials herein are protected by United States copyright law and may not  be reproduced, distributed, transmitted, displayed, published or broadcast  without the prior written permission of VIQ Media Transcription, Inc. You  may not alter or remove any trademark, copyright or other notice from  copies of the content. \par \par \uc2 Document INGANG0020241119ekbi00001\par }\page {\par\fs20\uc2 News; Domestic\par \b \uc2 Left Loses It Over \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's Cabinet Picks; Ending The Weaponization Of Government; Trump administration ready to prioritize America's health; Making American cities great again; Liberal commentator admits Democrats failed big cities; Democrats will resist Trump's most popular policies; Colorado governor says Operation \uc2 Aurora\uc2  would devastate economy; Dismantling the work education system; Hollywood elites don't want to live in America; Mass exodus, liberals are leaving the X platform\b0\par\par\uc2 Bret Baier, Laura Ingraham, Marc Siegel, Laura Ingraham, Marc  Siegel. Ben Domenech, Lisa Boothe \par \uc2 7,524 \uc2 words\par \uc2 14 November 2024\par \uc2 Fox News: The Ingraham Angle\par \uc2 INGANG\par \uc2 English\par \uc2 Copyright 2024 VIQ Solutions, Inc. \par \par \uc2 BRET BAIER, FOX NEWS HOST: Tomorrow on Special Report, how people who voted split tickets costs Republicans some Senate seats, we'll take a look. Plus, an in-depth look at what's happening in Pennsylvania with that Senate recount. Remember, if you can't catch us live, set your DVR, 06:00 p.m. the East, 03:00 p.m. on the West Coast. Thanks for inviting us into your home tonight. That's it for this Special Report. Fair, balanced and still unafraid. The Ingraham Angle starts now.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle reporting from Florida tonight. A flurry of new Trump nominations released today, one of his outside counsels, Todd Blanche, as his Deputy Attorney General. Former Congressman \uc2 Doug Collins\uc2  of Georgia for VA Secretary. And former Missouri Solicitor General, John Sauer, as S.G. Solicitor General of the United States. But first, consider the source. That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 All right, we knew it was coming, speaking of new picks, Trump picks, RFK Jr. to head the \uc2 Department of Health and Human Services\uc2 , and this only adds to the number of heads blowing off the shoulders of official Washington tonight. Now, the effort to discredit the RFK Jr. nomination has been underway ever since he endorsed Trump back in August. A Vox headline, "Trump really could empower RFK Jr. to wreck public health." From the New Republic, "Trump officially gives RFK Jr. a chance to destroy the country's health." And my personal favorite from the Arizona Public Health Association, "why RFK as \uc2 HHS\uc2  Secretary could mean the end of evidence-based public health policy."\par \par \uc2 OK, evidence-based health? How about this evidence? A record number of Americans are suffering from chronic illnesses. One in six adults now has diabetes, and by 2050, given current trends, about 61 percent of adults are predicted to develop cardiovascular disease. So RFK understands this is a ticking time bomb for our families, for our hospitals, our doctors, our nurses, our local, state and federal budgets. And all of this is happening, by the way, as we're spending more on health care than ever before.\par \par \uc2 Now in 2022 we have good, good numbers. We spent 4.5 trillion or $13,493 per person on health care. That's more than any developed nation, but without any better results. So speaking of evidence, logic would indicate that what we've been doing isn't working, and if so facto, we need a fresh perspective before we as a people get even sicker. But more fury and fear over the RFK nomination in a few moments.\par \par \uc2 But one thing again, we do know conclusively, the gatekeepers of the bureaucracy, whether it's at \uc2 HHS\uc2  or anywhere else, and those who get rich from the status quo in D.C. are always going to be threatened by anyone demanding accountability. And this explains a lot of the frenzy over Trump's recent cabinet picks. \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  as Director of National Intelligence, you think Trump had given it to Putin himself.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 OLIVIA TROYE, FORMER ADVISOR TO VICE PRESIDENT MIKE PENCE: We're bringing in Russia's influence is what this is. We have people like \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  who are spreading Kremlin talking points.\par \par \uc2 TOM NICHOLS, STAFF WRITER, THE ATLANTIC: She's an admirer both of both of \uc2 Bashar Assad\uc2  of Syria and an apologist for \uc2 Vladimir Putin\uc2  of Russia.\par \par \uc2 JOSH ROGIN, COLUMNIST, WASHINGTON POST: \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  has a long history of siding with the analysis of Russian state propaganda, Syrian state propaganda.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: They can't help themselves. Pete Hegseth at DOD. The MIC, Military Industrial Complex has gone to DEFCON 1 over this pick.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Pete Hegseth, inarguably, is not qualified for the position.\par \par \uc2 REP. TAMMY DUCKWORTH (D-IL): This idea that you can exclude women from combat is really one that shows his lack of experience and really him being unqualified to be the Secretary of Defense.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: He is the most unqualified candidate for this position in the history of America. This is very dangerous.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 's nomination as A.G., well, of course, that's already in serious trouble. Some even speculating that the nominee himself knew all along, it would be a long shot. I mean who knows. A House Ethics report on Gaetz was ready to be released on Friday, but since he resigned, well, the committee loses jurisdiction over the matter. Still Tricky \uc2 Dick Durbin\uc2  sees an opening to hurt Trump by forcing the reports released to the Senate, where, if past is prologue, we can all be sure that that content is sure going to leak. Trump's team had to know what the Hill reaction would this - - to this would actually be.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: A Republican friend of mine, who is also friends with \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 , told him (inaudible) he thought this appointment was the worst thing that's ever happened to the country.\par \par \uc2 ANDREW MCCABE\uc2 , CNN SENIOR LAW ENFORCEMENT ANALYST: This is the first step likely in Trump's revenge tour against the Department of Justice.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: He is the Exhibit A to weaponization. I mean, we are in pure George Orwell 1984 land.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Thank you, Andrew. Of course, we can't predict what's going to happen, or if this is a way to force the Senate to accept recess appointments. But incoming Senate Majority Leader \uc2 John Thune\uc2  is leaving all options on the table.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 SEN. \uc2 JOHN THUNE\uc2  (R-SD): And I always believe that you defer to a president when it comes to the people they want in their cabinet, and to do a lot of these important jobs, but obviously there is a process whereby we get down and scrub all these nominees and figure out whether or not one, they're qualified and are they people who are fit to hold these offices.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, I certainly hope that as they carry out their advise and consent role, Republican senators, remember, that \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is the reason they even have a majority. And as Republicans fight amongst themselves, perhaps Democrats plan to use every avenue to block Trump even forming, and they're admitting this a shadow cabinet.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: We can't let \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2 's extreme MAGA agenda go unanswered or unopposed. Zone defense isn't going to work. We're going to have to go man-on-man. We need to borrow from our British friends and appoint a shadow cabinet to fight back against the worst abuses of a second Trump administration. A team from the opposition that mirrors the government's own cabinet members. They watch the cabinet closely, publicly challenging, scrutinizing and offering new ideas. It's another form of checks and balances, a quiet guardrail that holds those in power accountable.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: It's another form of checks and balances. Was that in the Constitution, I must have missed that. I love when they bring their props, by the way. So this makes it even more critical for President Trump to have all his ducks in a row on the Hill before making big appointments. He's always been more effective that way. There's no time to waste. Well, all this plays out. We should also consider the source or sources of this incoming stream of criticism.\par \par \uc2 I mean, these people have been wrong about pretty much everything, propping up Biden's terrible cabinet picks just because they were first, first this or first that. Of course, with the help of their friends in the press.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 WOLF BLITZER, CNN HOST: President-elect \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  announcing historic picks for top posts in his cabinet, including former Federal Reserve Chair \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2  to be the country's first woman Treasury Secretary.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2 's cabinet nominees look like America, quite frankly, diversity in thought, diversity in race, in gender and everything. That is what America looks like.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: \uc2 Joe Biden\uc2  has appointed the most diverse cabinet in history.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: That's all that mattered. Forget qualifications, but that made them qualified because they were diverse. Made no sense. By the way, what did Mayor Pete do to qualify himself to run the Department of Transportation? Mayor of South Bend, really? What about Alejandro Mayorkas? His qualifications gave an invasion of illegal aliens to America.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ALEJANDRO MAYORKAS, SECRETARY, DEPARTMENT OF HOMELAND SECURITY: The message is quite clear, do not come. The border is closed. The border is secure.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: But even their credentials -- credentialed picks were like former Federal Judge \uc2 Merrick Garland\uc2 , when they weren't working on ways to harass Trump, they were catering to BLM extremists.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 MERRICK GARLAND\uc2 , U.S. ATTORNEY GENERAL: The top domestic violent extremist threat comes from racially or ethnically motivated violent extremists, specifically those who advocated for the superiority of the white race.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I forgot that was a golden oldie. And of course, we can't forget Biden's whiz bang economic expert \uc2 Janet Yellen\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JANET YELLEN\uc2 , U.S. SECRETARY OF THE TREASURY: We've had several months of high inflation that most economists, including me, believe will be transitory.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Transitory, it's still with us, writing, still writing articles about inflation today. Over the past few years, \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  was very clear that he wanted to finish the job he started in his first term. He intends to drain the swamp and restore trust and accountability in Washington. Now this won't be easy. The Washington bureaucracy has been around a lot longer than any of the committed, smart patriots, committed to undoing it.\par \par \uc2 The establishment may have lost this last election to MAGA Republicans, but it's still well-funded, and it's still committed to surviving even the reform efforts of \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 . Strategic thinking, strong nominees and well- placed allies on the Hill will make all the difference. The momentum is Trump's to lose or use for phenomenal achievement. As for the relentless criticism, always consider the source. And that's the Angle.\par \par \uc2 Joining me now is Alina Habba, Trump's Senior Advisor and Attorney. Alina, great to have you on tonight. I want to start with \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2 . What can you tell us about the process of choosing him to be A.G., was there a lot of consultation with the Hill? Did you all bring in Speaker of the House or any of the other top Republicans?\par \par \uc2 ALINA HABBA, SENIOR ADVISOR TO PRESIDENT TRUMP: I'm not part of the transition team, and as you know, Laura, I always take my confidentiality incredibly seriously, but I'll say this. \uc2 Matt Gaetz\uc2  is somebody that has always been on the President's radar. Has always been America First, whether the radical Left likes it or not. He has been very clear about who he is, and despite the bullying, which we've seen time and time again, and frankly, Laura, I'm shocked, they've only waited a couple days for more fear-mongering, which you just played for the American people.\par \par \uc2 You know, he's making selections on people that are not going to be bullied. And we have seen time and time again, political people who are career politicians come in. They act like they're Republican. They turn out to be a Rhino. They fold and buckle under pressure. These people, his selections, they're not that. And that might be frightening to the CNN's and MSNBC's and the people that put up charts and say that they will not respect the rule of law, the Constitution and the separation of powers, but they've got another thing coming. We need to respect the process. The President has to respect the people he's putting in these roles. And frankly, I do. I think he's made great decisions. I'm excited for what's to come. I think America spoke loudly that they were excited for what's to come on November 5th.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, Alina, John Brennan, one of our personal favorites, you know, who lied? The former CIA director who lied about \uc2 Hunter Biden\uc2 's laptop, had this to say about \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2 . Watch this.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 JOHN BRENNAN, FORMER CIA DIRECTOR: \uc2 Tulsi Gabbard\uc2  has taken actions and made statements over the past several years that really raised serious questions about her common sense, her judgment, as well as her political sympathies, cozying up to Putin as well as to meeting with \uc2 Bashar Assad\uc2 , I think really does show that she doesn't have the type of perspective that is needed for somebody who's going to head up these 18 intelligence agencies.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Alina, so now