o weeks ago. We'll tell you -- and fair, balanced and unafraid. We've got you covered.\par \par \uc2 LAURA INGRAHAM, FOX NEWS HOST: Good evening, everyone. I'm Laura Ingraham. This is The Ingraham Angle from Washington tonight. Happy Columbus Day, everybody. Well, this is a day that commemorates the discoveries and daring spirit of Christopher Columbus. Now, it's a figure that is revered especially by Italian Americans. But of course, as they do with every American tradition, the Left and \uc2 Kamala Harris\uc2  want to destroy this day and shame all of us for celebrating. Remember this gem?\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 KAMALA HARRIS\uc2 , VICE PRESIDENT OF THE U.S., (D) PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: It is an honor, of course, to be with you this week as we celebrate Indigenous Peoples Day, as we speak truth about our nation's history. Those explorers ushered in a wave of devastation for tribal nations, perpetrating violence, stealing land and spreading disease. We must not shy away from this shameful past.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Well, of course, Trump, he's sticking with Chris.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), FORMER U.S. PRESIDENT AND 2024 PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: His memory stands as an enduring testament to the daring spirit that built our great civilization. And as long as I have anything to say about this, and I hope that's going to be a long time, it will always be Columbus Day.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: And that is a perfect encapsulation of where we are as a nation, and the choice that's before us in 22 days. So, which way is it America? That's the focus of tonight's Angle.\par \par \uc2 All right, over the weekend, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's team of aerospace engineers and physicists managed to pull off two high risk dramatic feats. First, \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  launched a massive, super heavy starship rocket, which, in and of itself, was incredible to watch. But what happened after was truly mind-blowing. Now, the first stage of the rocket landed back on the launch pad with the help of a gargantuan mechanical arm and a cool pincer type move.\par \par \uc2 (VIDEO PLAYING)\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: We have successfully caught the Super Happy Booster back at the launch tower. What an incredible day.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Literally, the tower caught the rocket, as \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  tweeted. And then the other objective perfectly achieved was the spectacular belly flop, splashdown, right on target in the Indian Ocean, Sunday morning, after the successful test flight.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Starship is on target, approaching landing burn startup.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Landing burn start up.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: The reflection of that landing burn.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: You can see the walker just behind the ship.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED MALE: Starship has landed.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: An incredible deal, it's safe to say, we have a ship in the water.\par \par \uc2 UNIDENTIFIED FEMALE: Touchdown.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: I don't know if it was like this for you, but I could not get enough of this. It was absolutely awe-inspiring, and that was after Musk unveiled his \uc2 Robotaxi\uc2  prototype and his plans for a new \uc2 Tesla\uc2  robot last Thursday.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 ELON MUSK, CEO, \uc2 SPACEX\uc2 : It can be a teacher, babysit your kids. It can walk your dog, mow your lawn, get the groceries, just be your friend, serve drinks. I think this will be the biggest product ever of any kind.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Now, \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2 's success in innovation would not have been possible in a socialist country, but it's possible here, at least for now. But in states like California, this type of spectacular risk taking, and investment is becoming increasingly more difficult. Now, we all know that \uc2 Elon Musk\uc2  already announced his move of X and \uc2 SpaceX\uc2  from the Golden State where both companies were founded.\par \par \uc2 But the corporate exodus from California has been going on for years as other states like Texas, Tennessee, Florida, South Dakota, the list goes on, have been over backwards to create much friendlier business climates.\par \par \uc2 At its best, our capitalist system encourages risk taking and rewards smart innovation. It doesn't punish success with burdensome regulations or a crushing tax regime. Now, check out the top states for doing business in 2024 by one survey. So, what do nine out of 10 of them have in common, Republican governors.\par \par \uc2 But Harris and the Democrats, they have other priorities beyond just growing an economy or innovation. Well, they have climate change, of course, that's their religion, and then they want to wokeify everything we do, everywhere we do it. And when you need to get rockets up in the air and cars on the road that are self-driving, the last thing you should be thinking about is racial or ethnic quotas in hiring, it should never be thinking about that anyway. Hiring the best and most talented people is Musk's hallmark.\par \par \uc2 Now, as the most innovative force in America today, it is fitting that Musk is working hard to get Trump reelected. He knows that to be a country where greatness can still happen, where the American dream is still possible, we have to protect our sacred rights. We have to respect our Constitution and yes, our traditions matter. We need to give our people a reason to celebrate the American spirit, as millions did over the weekend watching these incredible advances in space travel.\par \par \uc2 Now, of course, liberals are used to having all the billionaires on their side, so they've been on a tear against Musk since h