ohn.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: They certainly going to need something along those lines to recover from this. Mike, thank you.\par \par \uc2 EMANUEL: You bet.\par \par \uc2 ROBERTS: If you would like to help those impacted by Hurricane Helene, you can donate now at redcross.org/foxforward, or simply scan the QR code on your screen.\par \par \uc2 Former President \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  is criticizing the Biden-Harris's administration response to Hurricane Helene, the Republican nominee was in Georgia today to distribute supplies and receive a briefing on the storm's impact.\par \par \uc2 Correspondent Alexandria Hoff is in Valdosta tonight.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEOTAPE)\par \par \uc2 DONALD TRUMP\uc2  (R), U.S. PRESIDENTIAL CANDIDATE: We pull together, we pitch in, we persevere.\par \par \uc2 ALEXANDRIA HOFF, FOX NEWS CHANNEL CORRESPONDENT (voice over): In the rubble of a storm wrecked antique mall. Former President Trump said he came to Valdosta with much needed supplies in tow.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP\uc2 : From oil to water to all sorts of equipment that's going to help them.\par \par \uc2 HOFF (voice over): In partnership with Franklin Graham's relief organization \uc2 Samaritan's Purse\uc2 , Trump said he stands in solidarity with the people of Georgia and plans to travel to North Carolina later this week.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: As you know, our country is in the final weeks of a hard fought national election, but in a time like this when a crisis hits, when our fellow citizens cry out in need, none of that matters. We're not talking about politics.\par \par \uc2 HOFF (voice over): But when asked if he has reached out to President Biden about federal relief efforts.\par \par \uc2 TRUMP: No, I haven't reached out to him. No, I think he's sleeping right now.\par \par \uc2 HOFF (voice over): Trump also accused the current administration of being unresponsive to Georgia Governor Brian Kemp. This morning, Kemp said that he did speak with President Biden after missing his ca