nia is a very important place. And it's -- I went to school here. I went to college here, as you know. And it's a great, great place. It's a fabulous place, the commonwealth. And we're going to make you very happy.\par \par \uc2 All of those things that we talked about are very easily solvable with you. I -- that's such an easy -- that could be done in one day. I had a cabinet maker. He said, sir, China and South Korea dropping cabinets into our country for nothing. And I can't compete.\par \par \uc2 And I studied it. And I ended up putting a 50 or 75 percent tariff for all cabinets coming into the country. And I didn't know the guy. He just -- I met him previous to going in to the presidency. And I saw him four years later. He said, sir, you saved my business, you saved the job, I expanded. They stopped with the dumping.\par \par \uc2 And the steel, the same thing. I think the steel people like me the best. Unfortunately, Biden's let it go. I put tariff -- they were dumping Chinese steel into our country, David, at levels that nobody's ever seen before. We have never seen anything like it. And I put a 50 percent tariff on all steel coming in from China and some other places too, but all steel.\par \par \uc2 And we saved these companies, but Biden has let it go. And we need steel. Look, there are some things you could get from outside, like a -- but if we're in a war and we need army tanks, and we need ships, and we need other things that happen to be made of steel, what are we going to do, go to China and get the steel? We're fighting China, but do you mind selling us some steel?\par \par \uc2 Think of it. These people don't know what they're doing. So I put big tariffs on steel. They were dumping steel. And it was bad steel too. It was rotted -- what -- called rotted steel, bad steel. It was imperfect steel. People were building girders for buildings and they check them and they're not good. The steel wasn't good.\par \par \uc2 But they were dumping at tremendous 