r \uc2 Court documents released today say Routh dropped off a box full of ammunition, four phones and various letters to a friend. One of the letters addressed "Dear World" discuss the failed assassination attempt, even going so far to offer money to finish the job.\par \par \uc2 Prosecutors will most likely argue this letter proves some sort of intent or motive. Law enforcement also found six cell phones in Routh's getaway car. One phone had a \uc2 Google\uc2  search of how to travel from South Florida to Mexico. Agents found a handwritten note of past and future Trump appearances, which suggests that he was tracking the former president.\par \par \uc2 Now, he is scheduled to appear in court next Monday for a probable cause hearing. This is where we can see the government lay out even more evidence against Ryan Routh -- Sandra.\par \par \uc2 SMITH: All right, Danamarie McNicholl live there in West Palm Beach for us, thank you.\par \par \uc2 The bipartisan task force assigned to probe the first attempted assassination of \uc2 Donald Trump\uc2  in Pennsylvania now has jurisdiction to probe this one in Florida.\par \par \uc2 The chairman of that force, Pennsylvania Republican Congressman Mike Kelly, joins us now.\par \par \uc2 Congressman, thank you very much for being here today.\par \par \uc2 So, first off, your reaction to today's developments.\par \par \uc2 REP. MIKE KELLY (R-PA): Well, I think this gets more and more complicated.\par \par \uc2 And yet, by the same term, it's more and more obvious that there's something afoot here. And so you have two instances, one in Butler, Pennsylvania, one in Florida, with the same final result being looked for is the assassination of President Trump.\par \par \uc2 You start to look at that and say, so how deep does this go? How does this happen? Who's making the different connection and who's planning the plans to get there? And the more we look, the more we find.\par \par \uc2 I think the one thing for us is, we are taking 