c2 Anthony Fauci\uc2  is back and he's hawking his new book. After all, who else would catalog this story about how wonderful and brilliant Fauci was during COVID? After supporting the lockdowns that robbed children of learning, forcing the elderly to die alone, and then the mandating of unnecessary experimental shots, Fauci was toasted by the same media cultists who even now miss their Zoom cocktail parties.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: You were guided by science always and telling the truth. And that still seems to have hurt you as we sit here today in 2024.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Just a few days ago your testimony down in Washington D.C. made headlines for the hostility that you received.\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: I feel like one of the things that I'm, sort of, counting on you, for now, is bearing a lot of slings and arrows that you don't deserve.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Let's face it, Fauci's missed all those accolades.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 UNKNOWN: Have you thought about running for president?\par \par \uc2 DR. \uc2 ANTHONY FAUCI\uc2 , \uc2 NIAID\uc2  FORMER DIRECTOR: No, no. No interest whatsoever.\par \par \uc2 People who throw dots at me, you know, think badly of me. But I'm fundamentally a pretty humble person.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: The only thing worse than being a braggart is being someone who just displays false humility. Joining me now, Dr. \uc2 Scott Atlas\uc2 , former Trump COVID advisor, senior fellow at the \uc2 Hoover Institution\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 Dr. Atlas, Fauci talked about how he would, you know, stand up to President Trump publicly during COVID, and then he took a shot. Watch.\par \par \uc2 (BEGIN VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 FAUCI: And then, when that didn't work, he started invoking magical cures like hydroxychloroquine, you know. And then when it became clear that wasn't working, he brought in \uc2 Scott Atlas\uc2  who told him everything he wanted to hear. And it was just wanting so much for it to go away and figuring out if it wasn't going to go away naturally, I'm going to act like it's going to go away. That was the problem.\par \par \uc2 (END VIDEO CLIP)\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Dr. Atlas, your response. Took a shot at you, my friend.\par \par \uc2 DR. \uc2 SCOTT ATLAS\uc2 , FORMER TRUMP WHITE HOUSE COVID ADVISER: Yeah. You know, Laura, if it weren't so morally repugnant to watch him, it would be comical. Let's be very clear here, Fauci's legacy is presiding over the biggest failure, the most immoral disaster of public health fiasco in history with his sidekick \uc2 Deborah Birx\uc2 .\par \par \uc2 And their legacy is very clear. It's not just the millions of people damaged, harmed and killed by his policies. It's not just the long-lasting damage on children, particularly, poor kids. It's also bigger things like personally destroying the trust in science and public health guidance. I'm not sure that's even reparable.\par \par \uc2 And lastly, I think people have to realize he is personally responsible for a lot of the hateful division among Americans with these pseudoscience mandates demonizing people.\par \par \uc2 And, you know, he was -- he made a fool out of himself, frankly, during the trial -- during the testimony the other day when he admitted there was no data on most of these mandates, and then they played his own words saying in an authoritarian way things like people lose their, quote, "ideological B.S.," unquote, when you make their lives difficult.\par \par \uc2 And you listen to Fauci say, listen, buddy, you want to go to school, you take the vaccine. Listen, buddy, you want to go to work, you take the vaccine. I mean, this is the sickest illustration of what happens when powerful people, what we call the elites, have disdain for regular people.\par \par \uc2 INGRAHAM: Yeah. And just going back to one of my favorite topics, other than the therapeutics that had clearly had